WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
Let's follow what AI contributes
to one banking release.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.960
Our example is a payment that
times out after acceptance.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:12.080
The customer retries, and the team
must prove that the money moves once.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.560
First, AI helps clarify the requirement.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.640
The product owner confirms
the expected behavior.

00:00:17.829 --> 00:00:22.400
Second, AI drafts the test
scenarios: normal payment,

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.600
timeout, repeated callback, concurrent
retry, and a conflicting request.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.440
Domain testers review the coverage
and expected outcomes.

00:00:31.953 --> 00:00:36.720
Third, AI helps developers write unit
tests for retry and duplicate-request

00:00:36.787 --> 00:00:40.400
logic. These are fast
checks of code behavior;

00:00:40.432 --> 00:00:42.641
they do not replace
payment integration tests.

00:00:42.937 --> 00:00:46.480
Fourth, AI turns accepted
cases into candidate

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.800
API and user-interface tests.

00:00:49.886 --> 00:00:52.400
Reviewers require
money-movement assertions,

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.280
not just a successful response.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.760
Fifth, AI helps draft synthetic data

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.880
and provider simulations.
Engineers validate them.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.760
Isolated environments and service
virtualization make the work repeatable.

00:01:06.647 --> 00:01:12.000
Sixth, AI recommends relevant tests
or requests an authorized pipeline run.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.880
The delivery pipeline executes the tests.

00:01:14.984 --> 00:01:17.840
Mandatory payment coverage stays in place.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.200
Seventh, AI connects failed assertions

00:01:21.232 --> 00:01:24.560
with logs and traces,
and drafts a diagnosis.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.720
The team checks the evidence
before accepting the explanation.

00:01:29.177 --> 00:01:32.080
Eighth, AI can propose a repair.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:37.360
A developer reviews the change, and the
pipeline reruns the tests with fresh data.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.400
The expected payment behavior stays fixed.

00:01:41.107 --> 00:01:45.520
Ninth, AI assembles a linked release
summary and suggests reviewed

00:01:45.582 --> 00:01:50.000
failures for the regression suite. People
decide whether the evidence is sufficient.

00:01:50.144 --> 00:01:55.120
That is the end-to-end opportunity: less
repetitive preparation and investigation,

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.960
supported by dependable
execution and accountable review.

00:01:59.056 --> 00:02:02.240
This is a proposed workflow
to validate in a pilot.
